namespace Pscf {
namespace Rp {

/*! 
\page rp_TrajectoryWriter_page TrajectoryWriter

This analyzer periodically writes the w-field configuration to
a trajectory file during a simulation, appending an additional
frame to file for each such configuration.  The resulting file 
can be read and analyzed after a simulation is completed by 
invoking the ANALYZE command.

\see TrajectoryWriter (class API)

\section rp_TrajectoryWriter_parameter_sec Parameter File

The parameter file format for the associated block is shown below:
\code
TrajectoryWriter{
  interval*        int     (1 by default)
  outputFileName   string
}
\endcode
Meanings of the parameters are described briefly 
below:
<table>
  <tr>
    <td> <b> Label </b>  </td>
    <td> <b> Description </b>  </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td> interval* </td>
    <td> number of steps between consecutive frames </td>
  </tr>
    <tr>
     <td> outputFileName </td>
     <td> name of output trajectory file </td>
  </tr>
</table>

\section rp_TrajectoryWriter_output_sec Output

During the simulation, the w-field configuration is output to file 
{outputFileName} every interval simulation steps.

The resulting file contains a header section followed by a sequence
of frames. The header has the same format as the header of an r-grid 
field file that holds a single field configuration. Each frame in a
trajectory file uses the same format as that used for the data 
section of an r-grid field file. 

*/

}
}
